# Crime Hotspot Prediction using Machine Learning

## Project Overview
This project analyzes crime data across Indian states and UTs to identify patterns and predict crime hotspots using machine learning techniques.

## Dataset Information
Compiled from NCRB Crime in India Reports (2019–2023) and BPRD data on police organizations.  
Covers 36 Indian states and UTs across 5 years with features including:

- Total IPC crimes  
- Violent, property, cyber, and women-related crimes  
- Conviction rate  
- Sanctioned vs actual police strength  
- Vacancy percentage  
- Police per lakh population  
- Police budget (₹ Crores)

*Note: Dataset not uploaded due to size constraints.*

## Technologies Used
- Python  
- Pandas, NumPy  
- Scikit-learn  
- Matplotlib / Seaborn  
- Jupyter Notebook  

## Objective
To analyze crime trends and build predictive insights for identifying high-crime regions and supporting data-driven policing decisions.

